  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nForecast messaging of dry weather amid anchored high pressure\nremains much of the same for the final days of the calendar\nmonth. Strong ridging aloft will slowly slide eastward through\nthe course of the work week, while at the surface, a backdoor \ncold front quietly passes over the area on Tuesday before \nlifting north as a warm front. Main implications to the \nforecast with this slight pattern change will then be a slight\nincrease in temperatures and less river valley fog and frost \npotential during the overnight hours as a result. Otherwise, \nprominently dry weather prevails today through the start of the\nweekend.\n\nThe ridge breaks down for the end of October, opening the door\nfor precipitation to return to the Ohio Valley. Model guidance\nsuggests this arriving in the form of a southern stream\ndisturbance late next weekend, with rain returning to the\nforecast for the first time in over a week.",
